{
 "encounter_id": "00985",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR",
  "person_3": "CAREGIVER"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Hello, doctor, I'm Beth, I care for Mr Calloway during the day. He's been coughing at meals, and he's frightened to eat."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thanks, Beth. Mr Calloway, can you tell me about it?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "It's, well, when I eat, or drink. It goes down the wrong way, and I cough."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Every meal, doctor. Even a cup of tea."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Does it feel like food sticks?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Sometimes, yes. In the throat, like it won't go down."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How's your voice after you've had a drink?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "It goes wet and gurgly. You can hear it."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any weight loss?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "No, not that I've noticed, we've been giving him milkshakes."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any chest infections recently?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. No chest infections."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What medicines is he taking?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Levothyroxine, 50 micrograms, every morning. And metoprolol, 25 mg, twice a day, I take both every day."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "It's 75 micrograms, Alf, the levothyroxine. And he forgets the evening metoprolol about three times a week."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I don't forget."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "We'll check the pharmacy about the levothyroxine. Any allergies?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "None. No allergies."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Medical history?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I had a stroke, two years ago. And the thyroid."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any dementia in the family?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "His mother had dementia, he told me."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Who's at home with him?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "His wife, and I come in at meal times."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me check your numbers. Pulse 74, blood pressure 138 over 82, temperature 36.7, oxygen 96 percent, breathing 16, weight 66 kilos.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Is that all right? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Noted. Any trouble with your breathing at rest, Mr Calloway?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, nothing at rest."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Here's what I think. The coughing at meals after a stroke, with the wet voice, suggests swallowing difficulty after the stroke."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Is that common? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Very. I'm also concerned that some food or drink may go into the lungs, so I can't rule out that it's already getting there."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is that serious? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It can be, which is why I'd like to arrange a swallowing assessment with a speech therapist, soon."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "When can he have it? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Within the week. Meanwhile, give him smaller, softer mouthfuls, sit him fully upright, and no straws."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "I'll do that. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "If he gets a fever, a new cough, or seems more breathless, ring us the same day."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "I will. Thank you, doctor. ~"
  }
 ],
